          "Q1. The monolithic rock-cut Kailasanatha Temple at Ellora (Cave 16), carved entirely from top to bottom out of a single rock cliff, was commissioned by which Rashtrakuta king?\n(a) Dantidurga\n(b) Krishna I\n(c) Govinda III\n(d) Amoghavarsha I\nCorrect Answer: (b) Krishna I [Explanation: Krishna I (8th century CE) commissioned the monolithic rock-cut Shiva temple of Kailasanatha at Ellora, one of the greatest engineering feats of ancient world rock architecture.]",
          "Q2. The Motupalli Inscription (Abhaya Sasanam), which granted safety and liberal customs duties to overseas maritime merchants sailing from foreign lands, was issued by which Kakatiya ruler?\n(a) Prola II\n(b) Rudradeva\n(c) Ganapatideva\n(d) Prataparudra II\nCorrect Answer: (c) Ganapatideva [Explanation: King Ganapatideva issued the famous Motupalli Charter in Guntur/Bapatla coast guaranteeing protection and fixed 1/30th customs duties to foreign merchants trading in pearls, horses, and silks.]",
