          "Q1. Who among the following historic personalities first unfurled the Indian National Flag on foreign soil at the International Socialist Conference held in Stuttgart, Germany in 1907?\n(a) Lala Har Dayal\n(b) Madame Bhikaji Cama\n(c) Shyamji Krishna Varma\n(d) Virendranath Chattopadhyaya\nCorrect Answer: (b) Madame Bhikaji Cama [Explanation: Madame Bhikaji Cama boldly unfurled the precursor to the Indian tricolor flag in Stuttgart in 1907, demanding international recognition of India's freedom.]",
          "Q2. The first registered widow remarriage in the Telugu-speaking region of Andhra was conducted by Kandukuri Veeresalingam Pantulu on which historic date?\n(a) 15 August 1878\n(b) 11 December 1881\n(c) 2 October 1893\n(d) 12 January 1885\nCorrect Answer: (b) 11 December 1881 [Explanation: Kandukuri performed the first widow remarriage in Andhra on 11 December 1881 at Rajahmundry, marrying Gogulapati Sreeramulu to Gowramma.]",
          "Q3. The Ghadar Party, an armed revolutionary organization aiming to liberate India from British rule, was founded in 1913 with its headquarters at San Francisco by:\n(a) V.D. Savarkar\n(b) Lala Har Dayal and Sohan Singh Bhakna\n(c) Ras Behari Bose\n(d) Sachindra Sanyal\nCorrect Answer: (b) Lala Har Dayal and Sohan Singh Bhakna [Explanation: The Ghadar Party was established in 1913 in the United States by Lala Har Dayal, Sohan Singh Bhakna, and other expatriate Punjabi immigrants at the 'Yugantar Ashram' in San Francisco.]",
