          "Q2. The earliest recorded stone inscription written entirely in the Telugu language is the:\n(a) Addanki Inscription of Panduranga\n(b) Kalamalla Inscription of Erikal Mutthuraju Dhanunjaya\n(c) Kurkyala Inscription of Jinavallabha\n(d) Bezwada Inscription of Yuddhamalla\nCorrect Answer: (b) Kalamalla Inscription of Erikal Mutthuraju Dhanunjaya [Explanation: Discovered in Kalamalla village, YSR Kadapa district, this Renati Chola inscription dates to 575 CE and is the earliest stone epigraph written entirely in Telugu.]",
