          "Q1. At which historic session of the All India Congress Committee (AICC) in 1921 did Pingali Venkayya submit his design of the National Flag to Mahatma Gandhi?\n(a) Kakinada Session\n(b) Vijayawada Session\n(c) Rajahmundry Session\n(d) Guntur Session\nCorrect Answer: (b) Vijayawada Session [Explanation: On March 31 \u2013 April 1, 1921, during the AICC meeting at Vijayawada, Pingali Venkayya presented the flag design, to which Gandhi added white and the spinning wheel.]",
          "Q2. Who led the famous Chirala-Perala non-cooperation struggle by organizing the entire population into a makeshift settlement named 'Nagarampalem'?\n(a) Tanguturi Prakasam Pantulu\n(b) Duggirala Gopalakrishnayya\n(c) Konda Venkatappayya\n(d) Parvataneni Veerayya Chowdary\nCorrect Answer: (b) Duggirala Gopalakrishnayya [Explanation: Duggirala Gopalakrishnayya ('Andhra Ratna') led the exodus of Chirala-Perala residents to Nagarampalem in 1921 supported by his Rama Dandu volunteers to protest municipal taxation.]",
