        "text": "The Andhra Pradesh Reorganisation Act, 2014 bifurcated the unified state into the successor states of Andhra Pradesh and Telangana with the 'Appointed Day' designated as June 2, 2014. The partition fundamentally disrupted Andhra Pradesh's fiscal structure, institutional infrastructure, and administrative apparatus due to the sudden loss of Hyderabad, triggering acute fiscal deficits, river water disputes, and long-standing political confrontations over Special Category Status (SCS)."
