          "Q1. Which critically endangered bird species, endemic to Andhra Pradesh and rediscovered in 1986, is protected exclusively in Sri Lankamalleswara Wildlife Sanctuary?\n(a) Great Indian Bustard\n(b) Jerdon's Courser (Kalivi Kodi)\n(c) Forest Owlet\n(d) Bengal Florican\nCorrect Answer: (b) Jerdon's Courser (Kalivi Kodi) [Explanation: Jerdon's Courser (Rhinoptilus bitorquatus) is a nocturnal ground-dwelling bird endemic exclusively to the scrub jungle of Kadapa, protected in Sri Lankamalleswara Wildlife Sanctuary.]",
          "Q2. Which is the largest Tiger Reserve in India by geographical area?\n(a) Jim Corbett Tiger Reserve\n(b) Nagarjunsagar-Srisailam Tiger Reserve (NSTR)\n(c) Bandipur Tiger Reserve\n(d) Manas Tiger Reserve\nCorrect Answer: (b) Nagarjunsagar-Srisailam Tiger Reserve (NSTR) [Explanation: Nagarjunsagar-Srisailam Tiger Reserve, spanning the Nallamala forest ranges across Andhra Pradesh, is the largest tiger reserve in India, covering over 3,700 sq km.]",
