        "text": "Andhra Pradesh's extensive 974-km coastline along the concave, warm waters of the Bay of Bengal renders it one of the most disaster-prone maritime states in South Asia. The state experiences recurrent tropical cyclones, devastating storm surges, coastal erosion, flash floods in the Godavari and Krishna basins, and chronic rain-shadow droughts across Rayalaseema, necessitating an integrated disaster management and environmental mitigation architecture."
