          "Q1. Which catastrophic cyclone struck the Diviseema region of Krishna district on November 19, 1977, resulting in over 10,000 fatalities due to a massive tidal surge?\n(a) Cyclone Laila\n(b) Diviseema Super Cyclone\n(c) Cyclone Hudhud\n(d) Cyclone Phailin\nCorrect Answer: (b) Diviseema Super Cyclone [Explanation: The 1977 Diviseema Cyclone was a Category 4 equivalent super cyclone accompanied by a 6-meter storm surge that decimated coastal villages in Krishna district.]",
          "Q2. The Doppler Weather Radars (DWR) operated by IMD to track coastal cyclones in Andhra Pradesh are installed at which two locations?\n(a) Kakinada and Tirupati\n(b) Visakhapatnam and Machilipatnam\n(c) Nellore and Guntur\n(d) Bapatla and Ongole\nCorrect Answer: (b) Visakhapatnam and Machilipatnam [Explanation: The India Meteorological Department (IMD) operates Doppler Weather Radars at Visakhapatnam and Machilipatnam for early cyclone detection and rainfall estimation.]",
