        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "The Constitution of India adopts the Westminster model of parliamentary democracy, establishing a bicameral Union Parliament (President, Council of States / Rajya Sabha, and House of the People / Lok Sabha under Article 79) and State Legislatures (Governor, Legislative Assembly / Vidhan Sabha, and optional Legislative Council / Vidhan Parishad under Article 168). While envisioned as the premier forum for representative deliberation, executive oversight, and national legislation, contemporary parliamentary functioning faces institutional challenges including declining sitting days, frequent disruptions, and bypass of committee scrutiny."
