          "Discuss the role and functioning of the Public Accounts Committee (PAC) and Departmentally Related Standing Committees (DRSCs) in ensuring executive accountability to the legislature. (APPSC Group-1 Mains, 10 Marks)\n-> Model Approach: Introduce parliamentary committees as the 'mini-parliament' enabling non-partisan, cross-party scrutiny away from public rhetoric; analyze PAC: scrutiny of CAG audit reports on appropriation and financial accounts, convention of Opposition leadership, checking financial impropriety and systemic leakages; analyze DRSCs (24 committees): in-depth examination of ministerial Demands for Grants, reviewing draft bills, holding executive officers accountable; discuss contemporary concerns (non-binding recommendations, bypassing committee referrals for fast-tracked legislation); conclude with recommendations from 2nd ARC and NCRWC.",
