          "Q2. Under Article 108 of the Constitution, who presides over a Joint Sitting of both Houses of Parliament?\n(a) President of India\n(b) Chairman of Rajya Sabha (Vice-President)\n(c) Speaker of Lok Sabha\n(d) Union Law Minister\nCorrect Answer: (c) Speaker of Lok Sabha [Explanation: Under Article 118(4), a Joint Sitting summoned by the President under Article 108 is presided over by the Speaker of the Lok Sabha (or in his absence, the Deputy Speaker).]",
