        "type": "list",
        "style": "numbered",
        "items": [
          "Examine the evolving role of Civil Society Organizations (CSOs) in shaping public policy and promoting participatory democracy in India. (APPSC Group-1 Mains, 10 Marks)\n-> Model Approach: Introduce civil society as the 'third sector' supplementing representative democracy; illustrate policy breakthroughs achieved through CSO agitation (MKSS leading to RTI Act 2005, Mazdoor campaigns for MGNREGA, Bachpan Bachao Andolan for child protection); analyze their role in grassroots monitoring (ASER report on education learning outcomes, social audits); critically examine challenges (opaque foreign funding scrutinized under FCRA 2020, professionalization gaps, conflicts with government development agendas); conclude on establishing structured state-civil society consultative mechanisms.",
          "Critically evaluate the significance of independent regulatory authorities in post-liberalization India. How do they balance consumer protection with market competition? (APPSC Group-1 Mains, 10 Marks)\n-> Model Approach: Explain the shift from state monopolies to an 'enabling regulatory state' after 1991; analyze core regulators: SEBI (capital market integrity), CCI (anti-cartel enforcement), and TRAI (telecom pricing and net neutrality); explain how they insulate economic regulation from political volatility; discuss institutional vulnerabilities: post-retirement appointment patronage, jurisdictional friction with parent ministries, and lack of specialized regulatory capacity; emphasize accountability to parliamentary committees.",
          "Discuss the constitutional role of the permanent Civil Services in a multi-party parliamentary democracy. How does 'Mission Karmayogi' aim to transform bureaucratic capability? (APPSC Group-1 Mains, 10 Marks)\n-> Model Approach: Outline constitutional architecture (Articles 309, 311, 312); analyze the core doctrines of political neutrality, professional integrity, and ministerial responsibility; examine structural challenges (politicization of transfers, procedural conservatism, siloed departmentalism); detail Mission Karmayogi's pillars (competency-based training framework, iGOT Karmayogi digital learning platform, shift from rules-based obedience to outcome-driven roles-based execution)."
        ]
