        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "Good governance signifies an exercise of administrative authority characterized by transparency, accountability, citizen responsiveness, rule of law, and equity. In India, democratic institutions have operationalized good governance through institutional mechanisms such as Citizen's Charters, statutory Right to Information (RTI Act 2005), Public Service Guarantee Acts, e-Governance delivery platforms, and grassroots Social Audits."
