        "items": [
          "Q1. Who was appointed as the first Chairperson of the Lokpal of India in March 2019?\n(a) Justice Dipak Misra\n(b) Justice Pinaki Chandra Ghose\n(c) Justice Ranjan Gogoi\n(d) Justice N. Santosh Hegde\nCorrect Answer: (b) Justice Pinaki Chandra Ghose [Explanation: Former Supreme Court judge Justice Pinaki Chandra Ghose was appointed as the first Chairperson of the Lokpal of India in March 2019.]",
          "Q2. The Central Vigilance Commission (CVC) was originally set up in 1964 following the recommendations of which high-level committee?\n(a) Gorwala Committee\n(b) Santhanam Committee\n(c) Sarkaria Commission\n(d) Kothari Commission\nCorrect Answer: (b) Santhanam Committee [Explanation: The Committee on Prevention of Corruption, chaired by K. Santhanam (1962\u20131964), recommended the establishment of the Central Vigilance Commission.]",
          "Q3. Under the Prevention of Corruption (Amendment) Act, 2018, which Section mandates prior government approval before conducting an investigation into an official decision of a public servant?\n(a) Section 7\n(b) Section 13(1)(d)\n(c) Section 17A\n(d) Section 19\nCorrect Answer: (c) Section 17A [Explanation: Section 17A, inserted by the 2018 amendment, provides that no police officer shall conduct any enquiry or investigation into any offence alleged to have been committed by a public servant relating to official recommendations or decisions without prior approval.]",
          "Q4. Which committee appointed in 1966 first recommended the establishment of a two-tier Ombudsman machinery named 'Lokpal' at the Centre and 'Lokayukta' in the States?\n(a) First Administrative Reforms Commission (1st ARC)\n(b) Second Administrative Reforms Commission (2nd ARC)\n(c) Law Commission of India\n(d) Sarkaria Commission\nCorrect Answer: (a) First Administrative Reforms Commission (1st ARC) [Explanation: The First Administrative Reforms Commission (1966), headed by Morarji Desai and later K. Hanumanthaiah, recommended the creation of Lokpal and Lokayuktas.]",
          "Q5. The principal seat of the Andhra Pradesh Lokayukta was established in which city pursuant to the 2019 legislative amendment?\n(a) Amaravati\n(b) Visakhapatnam\n(c) Kurnool\n(d) Vijayawada\nCorrect Answer: (c) Kurnool [Explanation: Following the AP Lokayukta (Amendment) Act 2019, the office and principal seat of the Andhra Pradesh Lokayukta was established at Kurnool in Rayalaseema.]"
        ]
