        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "The Indian legal system belongs to the common law tradition, anchored by constitutional supremacy. A foundational understanding of law requires mastering the distinction between substantive and procedural codes, the structural hierarchy of civil and criminal courts, statutory instruments such as decrees and orders, modern overhauls in criminal jurisprudence (including the Nirbhaya Act and the Bharatiya Sanhitas), and the rationalization of social welfare labour legislations into four unified Labour Codes."
