          "Explain the structural hierarchy of Civil and Criminal Courts in a district. Distinguish between the powers of a Sessions Judge and a Chief Judicial Magistrate (CJM). (APPSC Group-1 Mains, 10 Marks)\n-> Model Approach: Detail the district judicial pyramid; Civil hierarchy (District Judge, Senior Civil Judge, Junior Civil Judge); Criminal hierarchy (Sessions Judge, CJM, JMFC, JMFC-II); explain the distinct sentencing capacities: Sessions Judge can pass any sentence authorized by law (including life imprisonment and death sentence, with death sentence subject to mandatory High Court confirmation under Section 366 CrPC / 415 BNSS); CJM can pass sentences up to 7 years imprisonment and fines; delineate separation of judicial magistrates from executive magistrates under Article 50.",
