          "Q1. Under the Code of Civil Procedure (CPC), 1908, a formal adjudication that conclusively determines the rights of the parties with regard to all or any matters in controversy in a suit is defined as a:\n(a) Judgment\n(b) Order\n(c) Decree\n(d) Plaint\nCorrect Answer: (c) Decree [Explanation: Section 2(2) of the CPC defines a Decree as the formal expression of an adjudication that conclusively determines the substantive rights of the parties.]",
          "Q2. Under the Code of Criminal Procedure (CrPC), what is the maximum sentence of imprisonment that a Chief Judicial Magistrate (CJM) is legally competent to pass?\n(a) Up to 3 years\n(b) Up to 7 years\n(c) Up to 10 years\n(d) Life imprisonment\nCorrect Answer: (b) Up to 7 years [Explanation: Under Section 29(1) of the CrPC, the court of a Chief Judicial Magistrate may pass any sentence authorized by law except a sentence of death or imprisonment for life or imprisonment for a term exceeding seven years.]",
