        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "Government budgeting represents the primary sovereign instrument for macroeconomic stabilization, resource allocation, and income redistribution. In the Indian federal system, budgeting operates under constitutional parameters dividing taxation and expenditure jurisdictions between the Union and the States, mediated by quinquennial Finance Commissions and fiscal discipline legislation."
