          "Q1. Under Article 280 of the Indian Constitution, the Finance Commission is constituted by the President of India every:\n(a) 3 years\n(b) 5 years or earlier\n(c) 6 years\n(d) 10 years\nCorrect Answer: (b) 5 years or earlier [Explanation: Article 280(1) prescribes that the President shall, within two years from the commencement of this Constitution and thereafter at the expiration of every fifth year or at such earlier time as the President considers necessary, constitute a Finance Commission.]",
          "Q2. The concept of 'Effective Revenue Deficit' was introduced in the Union Budget of India on the recommendation of which committee/statutory amendment?\n(a) Kelkar Committee\n(b) FRBM Amendment Act, 2012\n(c) N.K. Singh Committee, 2017\n(d) Chelliah Committee\nCorrect Answer: (b) FRBM Amendment Act, 2012 [Explanation: Effective Revenue Deficit was formally introduced into the FRBM Act via the Finance Act/amendment of 2012 to exclude grants given to states for capital asset creation from the revenue deficit.]",
          "Q3. What is the vertical share of net divisible central tax pool recommended by the 15th Finance Commission (chaired by N.K. Singh) for the States?\n(a) 42%\n(b) 41%\n(c) 39%\n(d) 32%\nCorrect Answer: (b) 41% [Explanation: The 15th FC recommended 41% for states, retaining the 42% share recommended by the 14th FC minus 1% adjusted for the newly created Union Territories of Jammu & Kashmir and Ladakh.]",
          "Q4. Which constitutional provision empowers the Union Government to impose conditions and ceilings on borrowings by a State if the State has outstanding central loans?\n(a) Article 280\n(b) Article 292\n(c) Article 293(3)\n(d) Article 360\nCorrect Answer: (c) Article 293(3) [Explanation: Under Article 293(3), a State may not without the consent of the Government of India raise any loan if there is still outstanding any part of a loan made to the State by the Government of India.]",
