          "Explain the methodology adopted by NITI Aayog in computing the National Multidimensional Poverty Index (MPI). How does it differ from traditional consumption expenditure-based poverty estimation? (APPSC Group-1 Mains, 10 Marks)\n-> Model Approach: Define MPI using the Alkire-Foster method across 3 dimensions (Health, Education, Standard of Living) and 12 indicators; contrast with income/consumption expenditure poverty lines (Tendulkar/Rangarajan) which overlook non-monetary deprivations like clean drinking water, sanitation, and child mortality; detail how MPI captures acute deprivation intensity alongside headcount ratio; analyze the empirical results showing dramatic reduction in multidimensional poverty in India and Andhra Pradesh (below 7%).",
