          "Sir C.V. Raman (1888\u20131970): Discovered the Raman Effect (inelastic scattering of photons by molecules) on 28th February 1928 (celebrated as National Science Day); awarded the 1930 Nobel Prize in Physics; founded the Raman Research Institute.",
          "Dr. Homi J. Bhabha (1909\u20131966): 'Father of the Indian Nuclear Programme'; formulated India's unique Three-Stage Nuclear Power Programme; founded Tata Institute of Fundamental Research (TIFR) and Trombay Atomic Energy Establishment (now BARC).",
          "Dr. Vikram Sarabhai (1919\u20131971): 'Father of the Indian Space Programme'; established Physical Research Laboratory (PRL) and INCOSPAR (which evolved into ISRO); spearheaded the SITE (Satellite Instructional Television Experiment) in 1975.",
          "Dr. A.P.J. Abdul Kalam (1931\u20132015): 'Missile Man of India'; Project Director of India's first satellite launch vehicle (SLV-3); architect of Integrated Guided Missile Development Programme (IGMDP: Agni, Prithvi); 11th President of India.",
          "Srinivasa Ramanujan (1887\u20131920): Mathematical genius; profound contributions to analytical number theory, infinite series, continued fractions, elliptic functions, and mock theta functions (National Mathematics Day on 22nd December).",
          "Satyendra Nath Bose (1894\u20131974): Theoretical physicist; developed Bose-Einstein Statistics and predicted the Bose-Einstein Condensate; eponym of fundamental subatomic particles known as 'Bosons'.",
          "Sir M. Visvesvaraya (1860\u20131962): Renowned civil engineer and statesman (Engineers' Day on 15th September); engineered automatic sluice gates at Khadakwasla, Krishna Raja Sagara dam, and flood protection systems for Hyderabad and Visakhapatnam port.",
          "Dr. Yellapragada Subbarow (1895\u20131948): Andhra-born biochemist (from Bhimavaram); discovered the role of ATP (Adenosine Triphosphate) as the cellular energy currency, synthesized Methotrexate (first anticancer chemotherapy drug), Aureomycin (tetracycline antibiotic), and Hetrazan (cure for filariasis)."
