          "Trace the evolution of Science, Technology and Innovation (STI) policies in post-independence India. How does the Anusandhan National Research Foundation (ANRF) Act, 2023 aim to revolutionize R&D funding? (APPSC Group-1 Mains, 10 Marks)\n-> Model Approach: Trace chronological evolution: SPR 1958 (scientific temper, higher education), TPS 1983 (self-reliance), STP 2003 (market integration, PPP), STIP 2013 (inclusive innovation), and Draft STIP 2020; analyze India's persistent R&D deficit (Gross Expenditure on R&D stagnant at ~0.65% of GDP compared to 2-3% in US/China); detail the structure of ANRF: \u20b950,000 crore budget over 5 years (with ~70% targeted from private industry philanthropy/investments); explain how ANRF democratizes research grants across state universities beyond elite IITs/IISc.",
          "Highlight the contributions of Dr. Yellapragada Subbarow to medical biochemistry and pharmacotherapy. Why is he celebrated as one of India's greatest unsung scientists? (APPSC Group-1 Mains, 10 Marks)\n-> Model Approach: Introduce Dr. Yellapragada Subbarow hailing from Bhimavaram, West Godavari, Andhra Pradesh; detail his groundbreaking discoveries at Harvard and Lederle Laboratories: Fiske-Subbarow method for phosphorus estimation, isolation of ATP and phosphocreatine (vital for muscle contraction and cellular energy); explain his synthesis of Methotrexate (foundation of modern cancer chemotherapy) and aminopterin; detail the discovery of Aureomycin (first broad-spectrum tetracycline antibiotic saving millions of lives) and Hetrazan (diethylcarbamazine for curing lymphatic filariasis); conclude with his lasting legacy in global pharmacology.",
          "Evaluate the strategic role of Satish Dhawan Space Centre (SDSC SHAR), Sriharikota in India's space program and its technological significance for Andhra Pradesh. (APPSC Group-1 Mains, 10 Marks)\n-> Model Approach: Describe the geographical advantages of Sriharikota island in Tirupati district: coastal location allowing rockets to launch eastward over the Bay of Bengal (using Earth's rotational boost and ensuring debris falls into ocean), proximity to the equator; detail launch infrastructure: First Launch Pad, Second Launch Pad, Solid Propellant Booster Plant (SPROB), and integration facilities; discuss historic missions launched from SHAR (Chandrayaan-1/2/3, Mars Orbiter Mission, Aditya-L1, PSLV-C37 carrying 104 satellites); analyze regional economic and educational spillovers in Andhra Pradesh."
