        "items": [
          "Q1. National Science Day is celebrated in India on February 28 every year to commemorate which landmark discovery?\n(a) Discovery of Zero by Aryabhata\n(b) Discovery of the Raman Effect by Sir C.V. Raman\n(c) Launch of Aryabhata satellite\n(d) Pokhran-I Nuclear Test\nCorrect Answer: (b) Discovery of the Raman Effect by Sir C.V. Raman [Explanation: February 28 marks the day in 1928 when Sir C.V. Raman discovered the Raman Effect, which earned him the Nobel Prize in Physics in 1930.]",
          "Q2. The Anusandhan National Research Foundation (ANRF) Act, enacted by Parliament in 2023, replaces which existing statutory research body?\n(a) CSIR (Council of Scientific and Industrial Research)\n(b) SERB (Science and Engineering Research Board)\n(c) ICMR (Indian Council of Medical Research)\n(d) TIFAC\nCorrect Answer: (b) SERB (Science and Engineering Research Board) [Explanation: The ANRF Act 2023 repeals the Science and Engineering Research Board Act, 2008 and subsumes SERB into ANRF.]",
          "Q3. Which eminent scientist from Andhra Pradesh synthesized Methotrexate (the first anti-cancer drug) and discovered the cellular energy role of Adenosine Triphosphate (ATP)?\n(a) Dr. Yellapragada Subbarow\n(b) Dr. A.S. Rao\n(c) Sir C.V. Raman\n(d) Dr. Suri Bhagavantam\nCorrect Answer: (a) Dr. Yellapragada Subbarow [Explanation: Dr. Yellapragada Subbarow (born in Bhimavaram, AP) was a pioneering biochemist who discovered ATP and synthesized Methotrexate and Aureomycin.]",
          "Q4. Satish Dhawan Space Centre (SDSC SHAR), the primary space launch centre of ISRO, is located in which district of Andhra Pradesh?\n(a) Nellore\n(b) Tirupati (formerly part of SPSR Nellore)\n(c) Prakasam\n(d) Chittoor\nCorrect Answer: (b) Tirupati (formerly part of SPSR Nellore) [Explanation: Sriharikota is located in the newly carved Tirupati district (post-2022 district reorganization of Andhra Pradesh).]",
          "Q5. Subatomic particles that have integral spin (0, 1, 2) and follow Bose-Einstein statistics are named 'Bosons' in honour of which Indian scientist?\n(a) Homi J. Bhabha\n(b) Satyendra Nath Bose\n(c) Jagadish Chandra Bose\n(d) Meghnad Saha\nCorrect Answer: (b) Satyendra Nath Bose [Explanation: Paul Dirac coined the term 'Boson' to honor Indian theoretical physicist Satyendra Nath Bose for his pioneering work on quantum statistics.]"
        ]
