          "Explain the key architectural components of India's Digital Public Infrastructure (DPI) or 'India Stack'. How has it transformed financial inclusion and public service delivery? (APPSC Group-1 Mains, 10 Marks)\n-> Model Approach: Define DPI as digital rails that enable private and public service innovation; elucidate the 3-layer architecture: Identity Layer (Aadhaar), Payment Layer (UPI, IMPS, AePS), and Data Sharing Layer (DigiLocker, Account Aggregator); analyze impacts: elimination of leakages in DBT welfare schemes, exponential expansion of digital payments, formal credit delivery to unbanked street vendors (PM SVANidhi); discuss global adoption through G20 and challenges (digital divide, data privacy).",
