          "Q1. Under Section 70B of the Information Technology Act, 2000, which agency functions as the national nodal agency for responding to computer security incidents?\n(a) National Cyber Coordination Centre (NCCC)\n(b) CERT-In (Indian Computer Emergency Response Team)\n(c) National Critical Information Infrastructure Protection Centre (NCIIPC)\n(d) Cyber Crime Investigation Cell (CCIC)\nCorrect Answer: (b) CERT-In [Explanation: CERT-In is the designated national nodal agency under Section 70B of the IT Act for cybersecurity incident response and alerts.]",
          "Q2. What is the maximum financial penalty that can be imposed on a Data Fiduciary for failure to prevent personal data breaches under the Digital Personal Data Protection (DPDP) Act, 2023?\n(a) \u20b925 Crore\n(b) \u20b950 Crore\n(c) \u20b9100 Crore\n(d) \u20b9250 Crore\nCorrect Answer: (d) \u20b9250 Crore [Explanation: The Schedule to the DPDP Act 2023 prescribes a maximum penalty of up to \u20b9250 crore for failure of a Data Fiduciary to take reasonable security safeguards to prevent personal data breach.]",
