          "Q1. The HCF of two numbers is 11 and their LCM is 7700. If one of the numbers is 275, what is the other number?\n(a) 289\n(b) 308\n(c) 318\n(d) 328\nCorrect Answer: (b) 308 [Explanation: Product of two numbers = HCF * LCM. 275 * Other = 11 * 7700 => Other = (11 * 7700) / 275 = 7700 / 25 = 308.]",
          "Q2. What is the HCF of fractions 2/3, 8/9, 16/81, and 10/27?\n(a) 2/81\n(b) 80/3\n(c) 2/3\n(d) 16/81\nCorrect Answer: (a) 2/81 [Explanation: HCF of fractions = HCF(Numerators) / LCM(Denominators) = HCF(2, 8, 16, 10) / LCM(3, 9, 81, 27) = 2 / 81.]",
