          "Evaluate the exact numerical value of the expression without direct cubic computation: (0.7)^3 + (0.3)^3 - 3(0.7)(0.3)(1.0) / (0.7)^2 + (0.3)^2 - (0.7)(0.3). Formulate the identity proof. (APPSC Group-1 Mains Analytical, 10 Marks)\n-> Model Approach: Let a = 0.7 and b = 0.3. Then a + b = 1.0. We know the algebraic identity: a^3 + b^3 = (a + b)(a^2 - ab + b^2). The expression simplifies directly: [ (a + b)(a^2 - ab + b^2) ] / [ a^2 - ab + b^2 ] = (a + b). Since a = 0.7 and b = 0.3, (a + b) = 1.0."
