    "subject_title": "History and Culture of India",
    "raw_text": "Q4. In the Sangam literature, which ecological land classification (Thinai) corresponds to coastal maritime lands inhabited by fishermen and salt-makers?\n(a) Kurinji\n(b) Mullai\n(c) Marudham\n(d) Neydhal\nCorrect Answer: (d) Neydhal [Explanation: In classical Tamil poetics, Neydhal denotes coastal sandy tracts associated with fishing and salt manufacturing; Kurinji is mountainous, Mullai is pastoral forest, and Marudham is fertile agricultural river plains.]"
