    "topic_title": "European Trading Companies, Struggle for Colonial Supremacy & Governor-Generals and Viceroys",
    "subject_title": "History and Culture of India",
    "raw_text": "Q1. Which Indian ruler was the very first to accept the Subsidiary Alliance system formulated by Lord Wellesley in 1798?\n(a) Nawab of Awadh\n(b) Nizam of Hyderabad\n(c) Peshwa Baji Rao II\n(d) Raja of Tanjore\nCorrect Answer: (b) Nizam of Hyderabad [Explanation: Nizam Ali Khan of Hyderabad was the first Indian monarch to sign the Subsidiary Alliance treaty with Lord Wellesley in 1798.]"
