    "topic_title": "European Trading Companies, Struggle for Colonial Supremacy & Governor-Generals and Viceroys",
    "subject_title": "History and Culture of India",
    "raw_text": "Q2. The Treaty of Allahabad (1765), which granted the Diwani rights of Bengal, Bihar, and Orissa to the British East India Company, was signed by Robert Clive and which Mughal Emperor?\n(a) Farrukhsiyar\n(b) Muhammad Shah Rangila\n(c) Shah Alam II\n(d) Bahadur Shah I\nCorrect Answer: (c) Shah Alam II [Explanation: Following the decisive victory in the Battle of Buxar (1764), Robert Clive concluded the Treaty of Allahabad with Mughal Emperor Shah Alam II on 16 August 1765.]"
