    "topic_title": "European Trading Companies, Struggle for Colonial Supremacy & Governor-Generals and Viceroys",
    "subject_title": "History and Culture of India",
    "raw_text": "Q4. In which year was the historic Regulation XVII declaring the practice of Sati illegal and punishable as culpable homicide enacted by Lord William Bentinck?\n(a) 1813\n(b) 1829\n(c) 1833\n(d) 1856\nCorrect Answer: (b) 1829 [Explanation: Through the relentless efforts of Raja Ram Mohan Roy, Lord William Bentinck promulgated the Bengal Sati Regulation on 4 December 1829.]"
