    "subject_title": "History and Culture of India",
    "raw_text": "Q5. Which British Viceroy is revered as the 'Father of Local Self-Government in India' for his landmark Resolution of 1882 establishing rural and municipal local boards?\n(a) Lord Lytton\n(b) Lord Ripon\n(c) Lord Curzon\n(d) Lord Dufferin\nCorrect Answer: (b) Lord Ripon [Explanation: Lord Ripon's Local Self-Government Resolution of 1882 laid the foundation of representative municipal and local administration in British India.]"
