    "topic_title": "1857 Revolt, 19th Century Socio-Religious Reforms, Freedom Movement & Revolutionaries in India and Abroad",
    "subject_title": "History and Culture of India",
    "raw_text": "Q3. The Ghadar Party, an armed revolutionary organization aiming to liberate India from British rule, was founded in 1913 with its headquarters at San Francisco by:\n(a) V.D. Savarkar\n(b) Lala Har Dayal and Sohan Singh Bhakna\n(c) Ras Behari Bose\n(d) Sachindra Sanyal\nCorrect Answer: (b) Lala Har Dayal and Sohan Singh Bhakna [Explanation: The Ghadar Party was established in 1913 in the United States by Lala Har Dayal, Sohan Singh Bhakna, and other expatriate Punjabi immigrants at the 'Yugantar Ashram' in San Francisco.]"
