    "subject_title": "History and Culture of India",
    "raw_text": "Q5. The celebrated Telugu reformist drama 'Kanyasulkam', which fiercely satirized the social evils of child marriage, bride-price, and social hypocrisy, was authored by:\n(a) Kandukuri Veeresalingam\n(b) Gurajada Apparao\n(c) Gidugu Ramamurthy\n(d) Chilakamarti Lakshmi Narasimham\nCorrect Answer: (b) Gurajada Apparao [Explanation: Gurajada Apparao composed the landmark social satire play 'Kanyasulkam' in 1892, written entirely in colloquial spoken Telugu.]"
