    "subject_title": "History and Culture of India",
    "raw_text": "Q2. The military police action launched by the Indian Army in September 1948 to integrate the princely state of Hyderabad into the Indian Union was code-named:\n(a) Operation Vijay\n(b) Operation Polo\n(c) Operation Cactus\n(d) Operation Blue Star\nCorrect Answer: (b) Operation Polo [Explanation: Operation Polo was the code name of the military action launched on 13 September 1948 that liberated Hyderabad and integrated it into the Indian Union.]"
