    "subject_title": "History and Culture of Andhra Pradesh",
    "raw_text": "Q5. Acharya Nagarjuna, the propounder of the Madhyamaka (Sunyavada) school of Mahayana Buddhism, was a contemporary and friend of which Satavahana monarch?\n(a) Simuka\n(b) Gautamiputra Satakarni\n(c) Yajna Sri Satakarni\n(d) Hala\nCorrect Answer: (c) Yajna Sri Satakarni [Explanation: Tibetan and Chinese records, alongside Bana's Harshacharita, record that Acharya Nagarjuna resided at Sriparvata (Nagarjunakonda) under the patronage of Yajna Sri Satakarni.]"
