    "subject_title": "Indian Polity, Constitution and Governance",
    "raw_text": "Q1. Under Section 7(1) of the Right to Information Act, 2005, within how many hours must information be provided if it concerns the 'life or liberty' of an individual?\n(a) 24 hours\n(b) 48 hours\n(c) 72 hours\n(d) 7 days\nCorrect Answer: (b) 48 hours [Explanation: The proviso to Section 7(1) mandates that where the information sought concerns the life or liberty of a person, it shall be provided within 48 hours of receipt of the request.]"
