    "topic_title": "Good Governance, E-Governance, RTI Act, Citizen's Charter & Social Audit",
    "subject_title": "Indian Polity, Constitution and Governance",
    "raw_text": "Q4. Under which Act of Parliament was the conduct of regular Social Audits by the Gram Sabha made a mandatory statutory obligation?\n(a) Right to Information Act, 2005\n(b) Mahatma Gandhi National Rural Employment Guarantee Act (MGNREGA), 2005\n(c) National Food Security Act, 2013\n(d) Disaster Management Act, 2005\nCorrect Answer: (b) Mahatma Gandhi National Rural Employment Guarantee Act (MGNREGA), 2005 [Explanation: Section 17 of the MGNREGA, 2005 mandates that the Gram Sabha shall monitor the execution of works and conduct regular social audits of all projects within the Panchayat.]"
