    "topic_title": "Human Values, Attitude, Persuasion & Emotional Intelligence in Public Administration",
    "subject_title": "Ethics in Public Service and Knowledge of Law",
    "raw_text": "Q5. When an administrator demonstrates the capacity to listen attentively and genuinely comprehend the lived pain and perspective of a grieving citizen, they are displaying:\n(a) Sympathy\n(b) Empathy\n(c) Apathy\n(d) Antipathy\nCorrect Answer: (b) Empathy [Explanation: Empathy involves intellectually and emotionally understanding another person's lived experience and emotions from their own subjective viewpoint.]"
