    "topic_title": "Public Service Ethics: Codes of Conduct, Leadership Ethics, Anti-Corruption, Lokpal & Lokayukta",
    "subject_title": "Ethics in Public Service and Knowledge of Law",
    "raw_text": "Q3. Under the Prevention of Corruption (Amendment) Act, 2018, which Section mandates prior government approval before conducting an investigation into an official decision of a public servant?\n(a) Section 7\n(b) Section 13(1)(d)\n(c) Section 17A\n(d) Section 19\nCorrect Answer: (c) Section 17A [Explanation: Section 17A, inserted by the 2018 amendment, provides that no police officer shall conduct any enquiry or investigation into any offence alleged to have been committed by a public servant relating to official recommendations or decisions without prior approval.]"
