    "subject_title": "Economy and Development of India and Andhra Pradesh",
    "raw_text": "Q1. Under the Flexible Inflation Targeting framework adopted by the Reserve Bank of India, what is the official target for Consumer Price Index (CPI) Headline Inflation?\n(a) 3% with a tolerance band of +/- 1%\n(b) 4% with a tolerance band of +/- 2%\n(c) 5% with a tolerance band of +/- 1.5%\n(d) 6% with no tolerance band\nCorrect Answer: (b) 4% with a tolerance band of +/- 2% [Explanation: Section 45ZA of the RBI Act fixes the inflation target at 4% with an upper tolerance limit of 6% and a lower tolerance limit of 2%.]"
