    "subject_title": "Economy and Development of India and Andhra Pradesh",
    "raw_text": "Q2. What is the statutory time limit prescribed under the Insolvency and Bankruptcy Code (IBC), 2016 for completing the Corporate Insolvency Resolution Process (CIRP), including legal litigation?\n(a) 180 days\n(b) 270 days\n(c) 330 days\n(d) 365 days\nCorrect Answer: (c) 330 days [Explanation: An amendment in 2019 introduced a mandatory overall deadline of 330 days, including time taken in legal proceedings, for the completion of CIRP under the IBC.]"
