    "subject_title": "Science, Technology and Environment",
    "raw_text": "Q5. Which mangrove sanctuary in Andhra Pradesh, located at the mouth of the Godavari River, constitutes the second-largest mangrove forest in India after the Sundarbans?\n(a) Krishna Mangrove Sanctuary\n(b) Coringa Wildlife Sanctuary\n(c) Kambalakonda Wildlife Sanctuary\n(d) Nelapattu Bird Sanctuary\nCorrect Answer: (b) Coringa Wildlife Sanctuary [Explanation: Coringa Wildlife Sanctuary in Kakinada district encompasses the second-largest expanse of mangrove forests on the east coast of India.]"
