    "topic_title": "Biotechnology, Genetic Engineering, Nanotechnology, Vaccines, Infectious Diseases & Intellectual Property Rights",
    "subject_title": "Science, Technology and Environment",
    "raw_text": "Q2. The Nobel Prize in Chemistry 2020 was awarded to Emmanuelle Charpentier and Jennifer A. Doudna for the development of which revolutionary biotechnology method?\n(a) Polymerase Chain Reaction (PCR)\n(b) CRISPR-Cas9 method for genome editing\n(c) Direct DNA sequencing\n(d) Monoclonal antibody production\nCorrect Answer: (b) CRISPR-Cas9 method for genome editing [Explanation: Charpentier and Doudna discovered one of gene technology\u2019s sharpest tools: the CRISPR/Cas9 genetic scissors.]"
