    "topic_title": "Central Tendencies: Mean, Median, Mode & Weighted Averages",
    "subject_title": "General Mental and Psychological Abilities",
    "raw_text": "Q4. If every value in a dataset is multiplied by a constant factor k (k > 0), what happens to the standard deviation?\n(a) It remains unchanged\n(b) It increases by k\n(c) It is multiplied by k\n(d) It is multiplied by k^2\nCorrect Answer: (c) It is multiplied by k [Explanation: Multiplying all observations by a constant k scales the standard deviation by |k|, while the variance is scaled by k^2.]"
