    "topic_title": "Powers & Exponents, Roots, HCF & LCM Algorithms",
    "subject_title": "General Mental and Psychological Abilities",
    "raw_text": "Q2. What is the HCF of fractions 2/3, 8/9, 16/81, and 10/27?\n(a) 2/81\n(b) 80/3\n(c) 2/3\n(d) 16/81\nCorrect Answer: (a) 2/81 [Explanation: HCF of fractions = HCF(Numerators) / LCM(Denominators) = HCF(2, 8, 16, 10) / LCM(3, 9, 81, 27) = 2 / 81.]"
