    "subject_title": "Indian Polity, Constitution and Governance",
    "raw_text": "Explain the doctrine of Basic Structure as enunciated in the Kesavananda Bharati judgment (1973). How does it reconcile parliamentary sovereignty with constitutional supremacy? (APPSC Group-1 Mains, 10 Marks)\n-> Model Approach: Trace constitutional struggle between Parliament and Judiciary (Shankari Prasad -> Golaknath -> 24th Amendment -> Kesavananda); explain the 7:6 ruling on April 24, 1973; define Basic Structure (inalienable constitutional identity including democracy, secularism, rule of law, judicial review); explain how it harmonizes parliamentary power to amend against arbitrary subversion, establishing constitutional supremacy over legislative supremacy; cite Minerva Mills (1980) and NJAC judgment (2015) as subsequent applications."
