    "raw_text": "At what time between 4 o'clock and 5 o'clock will the hands of a clock be together (coincide)? Formulate the relative velocity derivation and evaluate the exact timestamp. (APPSC Group-1 Mains Analytical, 10 Marks)\n-> Model Approach: At 4 o'clock, the hour hand is at 4 (representing 20 minute spaces or 120 degrees ahead of the minute hand at 12). To coincide, the minute hand must gain 20 minute spaces over the hour hand. Since the minute hand gains 55 minute spaces in 60 minutes, the time required to gain 20 minute spaces is: Time = 20 * (60/55) = 20 * (12/11) = 240/11 = 21 (9/11) minutes. Alternatively, using the formula \u03b8 = |30H - (11/2)M| = 0: 30(4) - (11/2)M = 0 => 120 = (11/2)M => M = 240/11 = 21 (9/11) minutes past 4."
