    "subject_title": "General Mental and Psychological Abilities",
    "raw_text": "A 9-digit number 785x3678y is completely divisible by 72. Find the values of x and y (where y is the largest possible single digit), and calculate the value of (5x - 3y). Formulate the modular steps. (APPSC Group-1 Mains Analytical, 10 Marks)\n-> Model Approach: Divisibility by 72 requires divisibility by co-prime factors 8 and 9. 1. Divisibility by 8: Last three digits '78y' must be divisible by 8. 78y / 8: 780/8 = 97 rem 4, so 784/8 = 98 (rem 0). Thus y must be 4 (y=4 is unique single digit). 2. Divisibility by 9: Sum of digits must be divisible by 9. Sum = 7 + 8 + 5 + x + 3 + 6 + 7 + 8 + y = 44 + x + 4 = 48 + x. For 48 + x to be divisible by 9, x must be 6 (since 48 + 6 = 54). Therefore, x = 6 and y = 4. 3. Evaluation: (5x - 3y) = 5(6) - 3(4) = 30 - 12 = 18."
